, an absent query result, and a separate explicitly empty query; reopen identical. This remains a small synthetic sample, not proof of general fidelity.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNarrow live activation returned :compaction-prompt-activated: evaluated only slopchat--compaction-task. Newly prepared tasks use the correction; existing prepared jobs and historical canonical summaries are unchanged. No restart, full reload, agents, commit, reference edits, canonical-memory rewrite, or ledger reset.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") (write-region (point-min) (point-max) path nil 'silent))) (slopchat-run-command \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"git diff --check\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/workspace/formal-proofs/slopchat\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 10000))\\\\\\\"}}\\\",\\\"page\\\":0,\\\"pages\\\":1,\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-10-11T05:58:17.682Z\\\"}\"") ((0 7258) :summary "echo: Added the “Nested-result and author correction, 2026-10-11” section to `docs/memory-audit.md` and `docs/memory-handoff.md`. It records prompt-contract fixes, ERT 129/129, synthetic fixture outcomes and limitations, narrow activation, and actions not taken. `git diff --check` was run; its result is not stated." :source "echo: {\"id\":7242,\"kind\":\"tool\",\"text\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"emacs_eval\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"expression\\\":\\\"(progn (dolist (path '(\\\\\\\"/workspace/formal-proofs/slopchat/docs/memory-audit.md\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"/workspace/formal-proofs/slopchat/docs/memory-handoff.md\\\\\\\")) (with-temp-buffer (insert-file-contents path) (goto-char (point-max)) (insert \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Nested-result and author correction, 2026-10-11\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTask-local compaction instructions now preserve authoritative source author labels, distinguish quoted/nested payloads from outer results, exclude compaction instructions from source facts, and distinguish missing/pending results from explicitly empty collections. Added slopchat-compaction-nested-result-instructions (prompt-contract regression, not a semantic guarantee). Combined isolated ERT passed 129/129; log /tmp/memory-nested-final-ert.log.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nProduction-model fixture /tmp/slopchat-quality-nested.el exposed request-instruction leakage and a tool-to-user attribution error during intermediate runs; both prompted further corrections. Initial run failed with Connection closed, not a quality pass. Final run /tmp/slopchat-quality-nested-author.log preserved all four leaf authors, two entries with nil/pending summaries, an absent query result, and a separate explicitly empty query; reopen identical. This remains a small synthetic sample, not proof of general fidelity.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNarrow live activation returned :compaction-prompt-activated: evaluated only slopchat--compaction-task. Newly prepared tasks use the correction; existing prepared jobs and historical canonical summaries are unchanged. No restart, full reload, agents, commit, reference edits, canonical-memory rewrite, or ledger reset.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\") (write-region (point-min) (point-max) path nil 'silent))) (slopchat-run-command \\\\\\\"git diff --check\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"/workspace/formal-proofs/slopchat\\\\\\\" 10000))\\\"}}\",\"page\":0,\"pages\":1,\"date\":\"2026-10-11T05:58:17.682Z\"}") ((2 1812) :summary "tool: `emacs_eval` queried `(zoom 7202 1 0)`; tool: zoom returned the read-only spot-check report. echo: It found misattribution at `(3 896)`, a false “no entries” claim at `(2 1796)` despite entries (some pending) in message 7185, and a dropped outer query result in leaf `(0 7185)`. Findings were recorded in `docs/memory-audit.md` and `docs/memory-handoff.md`. Bounded check, not a quality guarantee; no canonical rewrites, restart, reload, or provider calls." :source "tool: {\"name\":\"emacs_eval\",\"input\":{\"expression\":\"(zoom 7202 1 0)\"}}
